{
  "The commands around the tabs: context menus on tabs and on the empty strip, a searchable list of a group's documents, the app's own toolbar buttons, the recently used list, back and forward, reopening what was closed, locked groups, and the keys for all of them.": "",
  "Context menus": "",
  "Every tab has the commands of its document, the empty strip those of its group. `menuItems` leaves built-in items out; `onContextMenuOpening` changes the list for each document or cancels it. `newDocument` makes a document for a double click on the empty strip.": "",
  "Command": "",
  "Item": "",
  "Note": "",
  "Close": "",
  "The tab; its key is shown next to it.": "",
  "Close others / to the right / to the left / saved / all": "",
  "Pinned tabs stay while `keepPinned` is on.": "",
  "Copy the title": "",
  "To the clipboard.": "",
  "Keep open": "",
  "Only on a preview tab.": "",
  "Pin / Unpin": "",
  "Whichever applies.": "",
  "Split up / down / left / right": "",
  "A new group on that side with the document (or a copy, see `splitCopies`).": "",
  "Move to the next / previous group": "",
  "Splits when there is no group that way.": "",
  "Move to…": "",
  "Chooses where the tab goes with the keys ([Drag and drop](/tabdocs/drag#keys)).": "",
  "Move group to… (empty strip)": "",
  "The same for the whole group.": "",
  "New document (empty strip)": "",
  "Only with `newDocument`.": "",
  "Reopen closed (empty strip)": "",
  "Dimmed while nothing can be reopened.": "",
  "Lock group / Unlock group (empty strip)": "",
  "The open documents list and toolbar buttons": "",
  "The “…” button (or Ctrl+K Ctrl+P) lists the group's documents, or every group's with `openListScope: 'all'`: type to search, Enter opens. `toolbarItems` adds the app's buttons to every group; a document's `actions` show while it is the active one.": "",
  "Recently used, back and forward, reopen": "",
  "The recently used list switches between documents the way code editors do with Ctrl+Tab. `goBack` and `goForward` follow the documents activated in every group; `reopenClosed` opens the last closed one where it was.": "",
  "Locked groups": "",
  "`lock(group)` keeps a group for what is in it: `open` without a group goes to another one, or to a new group beside it when all are locked (a single group still takes it). The lock is saved with the layout.": "",
  "A page in a browser tab never receives Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+T, Ctrl+Page Up / Down and often Ctrl+1…9: the browser keeps them. So a manager starts with keys that reach it there, the way the web version of the editor picks them (Ctrl+Alt for a Ctrl the browser keeps; Ctrl+E, the quick-open key, for the recent list), and keeps the desktop key as a second one. An installed app (display mode standalone) gets every key: there `keyPreset: 'auto'` takes `TabDocumentManager.desktopKeys`. `keys` changes any of them; an empty list turns one off.": "",
  "Browser tab": "",
  "Installed app": "",
  "Ctrl + W, Ctrl + F4": "",
  "Ctrl + Page Down / Page Up": "",
  "The next / previous tab (`nextTab`, `previousTab`).": "",
  "Ctrl + 1 … 9": "",
  "Focuses a group (`focusGroup`).": "",
  "Ctrl + Tab, Ctrl + Shift + Tab": "",
  "The recently used list: opens it, then walks it while Ctrl is held; letting go opens the highlighted document (`recentNext`, `recentPrevious`).": "",
  "Back and forward (`goBack`, `goForward`).": "",
  "Ctrl + Shift + T": "",
  "Reopens the document closed last (`reopenClosed`).": "",
  "Closes the group's documents / the saved ones (`closeAllTabs`, `closeSavedTabs`).": "",
  "Keeps a preview tab (`keepOpen`).": "",
  "Pins or unpins the active document (`togglePin`).": "",
  "Opens the \"…\" list (`showOpenList`).": "",
  "Splits to the right (`splitRight`).": "",
  "The context menu of the focused tab.": "",
  "The kit's `ContextMenu`: a `menu` opened by the right button, Shift+F10 or the Menu key on a tab, named after the document (or the group, on the strip); focus goes back to the tab when it closes.": "",
  "One menu: a search field, the documents as a `menu` named “Open documents” (`menuitemradio` items, the shown one checked; the description, the group and unsaved changes are said with each one) and the `menu` of commands. Up and Down go on from the search through the documents and the commands; typing on a document goes back to the search; Tab goes from part to part; Enter opens; Escape closes.": "",
  "The same menu of documents, named “Recently used documents”, with focus on the highlighted document, so it is read as it moves. It works without holding a key: the arrows move, a letter goes to a title, Enter opens, Escape closes.": "",
  "A locked group is named “Group 1, locked”; its toolbar has an “Unlock group” button.": "",
  "Locked and unlocked are said politely, like the other changes.": "",
  "The context menus of tabs and of the empty strip.": "",
  "`false` leaves a built-in item out: `{ copyTitle: false }`.": "",
  "The \"…\" button in each group's toolbar.": "",
  "Whether the \"…\" list and the recently used list show the group's documents or every group's.": "",
  "The app's buttons in every group's toolbar, made once per group (text, `icon`, `hint`, `tone`, `visible`, `enabled`, `click`…).": "",
  "Makes a new document for a double click on the empty strip and for the strip menu.": "",
  "How many activated documents `goBack` remembers; 0 turns the history off.": "",
  "How many closed documents `reopenClosed` remembers; 0 turns it off. Only documents whose content can be made again (a `content` function, the `factory`, a copy) are kept.": "",
  "Which keys the manager starts with (see Keyboard); `auto` takes the desktop keys when the page runs installed.": "",
  "The split, maximize and \"…\" buttons.": "",
  "Buttons in the group's toolbar while this document is the active one, before the built-in ones.": "",
  "Opens a group's \"…\" list: the documents to search and open, close all, close saved, lock or unlock.": "",
  "Opens the recently used list with the next document (or, with `-1`, the last) highlighted.": "",
  "The document activated before (or after) the current one, in whatever group. `canGoBack`, `canGoForward` say whether there is one (reactive).": "",
  "Opens the document closed last again, in its group and place. `closedDocuments` lists them (reactive).": "",
  "Also `group.lock()`, `group.unlock()`; `group.locked` reads it.": "",
  "Makes a document with `newDocument` and opens it.": "",
  "`'next'`, `'previous'`, or the group on a side (`'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'`, `'down'`); splits when there is no group that way.": "",
  "Writes the title to the clipboard.": "",
  "The open documents of every group, the one activated last first.": "",
  "`{ document, group, items, byKeyboard }`, cancelable; `document` is `null` for the empty strip. Change `items` (each built-in one has its command in `data`) or add your own.": "",
  "`{ group, byUser }`; the `…ing` ones are cancelable.": "",
  "The rest of the API is on the [overview](/tabdocs#api); preview and pinned tabs, sizes and copies on [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs).": ""
